    "evenflo_faq_aAgKwd": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_Xnt8cB": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the Revolve360™ Slim be used without cup holders?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, you can use this product without the cup holders attached to the car seat. The Revolve360™ Slim is all about flexibility and convenience. The cup holders are even safe to be placed in the top rack of your dishwasher for cleaning.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_AbTzPQ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I purchase an extra base?",
            "content": "<p>No, the shell and seat are designed to be used as a system and an extra base is not available for sale.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_PHg8zj": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I use the Revolve360™ Slim without the base?",
            "content": "<p>No — the car seat shell MUST be used with the base.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_FbNg67": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I know when the Revolve360™ Slim is locked into place?",
            "content": "<p>The red/green Seat Lock Indicator is a fast, easy way to make sure your Revolve360™ Slim is locked into place. The indicator will turn green when the seat is locked in the rear-facing or forward-facing position. The indicator must show green at all times when the vehicle is in motion.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_A84n8k": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Will the Revolve360™ Slim rotate on its own?",
            "content": "<p>No, as long as the product is correctly locked in the rear-facing or forward-facing position. You can confirm this by checking the Seat Lock Indicator on either side of the car seat — it will be green when in the locked position. In the interest of safety, only the caregiver should rotate the car seat by squeezing the rotation handle on either side of the car seat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_thTKfr": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Since the Revolve360™ Slim rotates, how do I know it won’t rotate on its own?",
            "content": "<p>You will find indicators on either side of the base, allowing you to easily check the car seat’s rotation lock status. The indicator will be green when in the locked position. The indicator must show green at all times when the vehicle is in motion.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_ErBWRn": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Does the Revolve360™ Slim move when the car is in motion because of the rotational feature?",
            "content": "<p>No, the Revolve360™ Slim is designed to be safe and secure when you’re on the go. You will find indicators on either side of the base, allowing you to easily check the car seat’s rotation lock status. The indicator will be green when in the locked position. The indicator must show green at all times when the vehicle is in motion.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_Ky9tYJ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is it possible for another child (sitting next to the seat) to make the Revolve360TM Slim rotate while I’m driving?",
            "content": "<p>When the vehicle is in motion, the car seat should always be correctly locked in the rear-facing or forward-facing position. You can confirm this by checking the Seat Lock Indicator on either side of the car seat — it will be green when in the locked position. Only the caregiver should rotate the car seat by squeezing the rotation handle on either side of the car seat. (Older children seated near the car seat should be instructed not to make any adjustments to the car seat).</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_fNE8qL": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Do the rotational components of the Revolve360™ Slim wear over time?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360™ Slim has been tested to meet strict cycling and durability standards, so it’s built to take you through childhood.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_wMTi7W": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the Revolve360™Slim use any other style LATCH/UAS?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360™ Slim should only be used with LATCH/UAS that is included with your purchase.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_KYctmd": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can the Revolve360™Slim use any other style LATCH/UAS?",
            "content": "<p>The Revolve360™ Slim should only be used with LATCH/UAS that is included with your purchase.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
