    "evenflo_faq_yWWYzX": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_n9XQEH": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I wash my Revolve360™ Slim padding? If so, how?",
            "content": "<p>Yes! For your convenience, the soft goods on your Revolve360™ Slim are washable.</p><p>This includes the seat pad, head pillow, body pillow, harness covers and buckle cover. Machine-wash separately in cold water on delicate cycle. Do not use chlorine bleach. Tumble dry on low heat for 10 – 15 minutes. Do not iron or dry clean. See product instructions for full cleaning details or watch our handy how-to videos: https://youtu.be/6ev2iRM_O00</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_GUcNJ9": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Can I safely disinfect my Revolve360™ Slim car seat?",
            "content": "<p>Evenflo allows the use of 70% isopropyl alcohol to disinfect car seat and booster seat surfaces, including the fabric, harness, buckle, plastic parts, foam and labels. You may spray or wipe the 70% isopropyl alcohol to dampen, but not soak, the surfaces. Afterwards, be sure to let the surfaces air dry. This guidance applies to all Evenflo car seats and booster seats. But keep in mind — this guidance does not apply to vehicle surfaces, like the seat belt. Please consult your vehicle manufacturer for guidance on disinfecting or cleaning vehicle surfaces.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_KNU6dd": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How easy is it to remove the seat pad to wash?",
            "content": "<p>Really simple! The seat pad is designed to be easy to remove and toss in the wash (just be sure to wash separately, delicate cycle, with mild detergent). See product instructions for full cleaning details or watch our handy how-to videos: <strong>https://youtu.be/6ev2iRM_O00</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_GExrgP": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How do I clean the plastic components of the car seat or base?",
            "content": "<p>Plastic components may be wiped clean with warm water and mild soap. Take care not to soak the product use labels.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
